mochiWM

Minimal X11 window manager in C. Ratpoison-inspired frames, Emacs-inspired keys

Keys

Press C-t, release it, then press a key below

C- means Ctrl; M- means Alt

Key          Action
2 / 3        Split top/bottom / side by side
0 / 1        Delete frame / keep only this frame
o / M-o      Next / previous frame
C-n / C-p    Next / previous window
C-b / b      List windows / select by number
M-! / k      Run program / close window
M-x          Command prompt
?            Active keybindings

C-g or Escape cancels a sequence or prompt

Commands

Open with C-t M-x, type a command, then press Return

exec xterm
select 2
split-vertical
reload-config
quit
restart

Backspace deletes a character. C-u clears the prompt

Configuration

Edit ~/.mochirc. Defaults work without this file

prefix C-t

bind Return exec alacritty
bind e exec firefox
bind R reload-config

exec feh --no-fehbg --bg-fill "$HOME/Images/wallpaper.jpg"
